(7354198, 1150005, 1031, '<td valign="top">Like someone said another title might have increased the score, but the photo is fine -- make sure she knows we (some of us, anyway) appreciate her effort -- you may have gotten only one good shot, but it''s a good shot ...</td>', 'Like someone said another title might have increased the score, but the photo is fine -- make sure she knows we (some of us, anyway) appreciate her effort -- you may have gotten only one good shot, but it''s a good shot ...', '2015-05-27 16:20:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354206, 1150005, 150277, '<td valign="top">I thought this shot was wonderfully funny, and the t-shirt helped match up to the title for me.  The lighting was a bit flatter than those that I scored most highly in this challenge, but it was a 6 from me.  But great model, very dramatic young lady. I admit I was a bit saddened to learn this wasn''t just a random youngster off the street flipping off a photographer.</td>', 'I thought this shot was wonderfully funny, and the t-shirt helped match up to the title for me.  The lighting was a bit flatter than those that I scored most highly in this challenge, but it was a 6 from me.  But great model, very dramatic young lady. I admit I was a bit saddened to learn this wasn''t just a random youngster off the street flipping off a photographer.', '2015-05-27 16:26:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354216, 1150005, 16106, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of those long ago handbills for punk shows. Both in content (youth don''t five a f*ck about you) and the high contrast in your face editing (a look that started because of printing on cheap paper for mass distribution, and became a it''s own aesthetic). I like it alot.<br/>That said, if you actually care about getting a higher score on this site I have started looking at my editing here as I do for my cooking at a dinner party. Have a little something for everyone, and spice to soften and fill out flavors rather than to heighten one flavor. If you had edited this as if it was a glamour shot with a soft glow to the skin and lots of pretty detail in the bricks, I bet it would have done about 6.2. Harsh shot gets soft edit, soft shot gets harsh edit, so you can please more of the people, more of the time. <br/>Now I need to get a shot of my daughter flipping off the camera in a challenge and see if I can do it so it offends fewer people by making the edit sweet enough to send diabetics into a coma.<br/>Or you can just go with the old punk philosophy, if they don''t like it, f#uck those people, this is our music!</td>', 'This reminds me of those long ago handbills for punk shows. Both in content (youth don''t five a f*ck about you) and the high contrast in your face editing (a look that started because of printing on cheap paper for mass distribution, and became a it''s own aesthetic). I like it alot.That said, if you actually care about getting a higher score on this site I have started looking at my editing here as I do for my cooking at a dinner party. Have a little something for everyone, and spice to soften and fill out flavors rather than to heighten one flavor. If you had edited this as if it was a glamour shot with a soft glow to the skin and lots of pretty detail in the bricks, I bet it would have done about 6.2. Harsh shot gets soft edit, soft shot gets harsh edit, so you can please more of the people, more of the time. Now I need to get a shot of my daughter flipping off the camera in a challenge and see if I can do it so it offends fewer people by making the edit sweet enough to send diabetics into a coma.Or you can just go with the old punk philosophy, if they don''t like it, f#uck those people, this is our music!', '2015-05-27 16:54:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354311, 1150005, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought everything about this worked very well together - the location, the way she''s posed in that space, her outfit - it all matches up to her attitude.  Your commenter average was significantly higher than your overall average - that''s usually a pretty good sign that you really struck a chord with a group of people - and that''s awesome!</td>', 'I thought everything about this worked very well together - the location, the way she''s posed in that space, her outfit - it all matches up to her attitude.  Your commenter average was significantly higher than your overall average - that''s usually a pretty good sign that you really struck a chord with a group of people - and that''s awesome!', '2015-05-27 20:05:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354359, 1150127, 86447, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous image, Mary Ann!  Congratulations on your ribbon!<br/></td>', 'Gorgeous image, Mary Ann!  Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2015-05-27 21:24:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354360, 1149936, 86447, '<td valign="top">Nicely done!   This was one of my faves of the challenge.  <br/> <br/>But, now I''m so jealous that you got to meet MAK and Wife that I can''t see it.  :D<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your ribbon and your experience!<br/></td>', 'Nicely done!   This was one of my faves of the challenge.   But, now I''m so jealous that you got to meet MAK and Wife that I can''t see it.  :D Congratulations on your ribbon and your experience!', '2015-05-27 21:25:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7354953, 1150127, 19825, '<td valign="top">I love how you''ve crafted such a lovely image out of such a simple scene. Recognizing the potential from an image you describe as rather dull is impressive. I need to learn a lot more about curve adjustment -- I don''t generally mess around with it. You have not only ribboned with an iPhone camera, but one that is a couple of generations old. Nicely done, Mary Ann.</td>', 'I love how you''ve crafted such a lovely image out of such a simple scene. Recognizing the potential from an image you describe as rather dull is impressive. I need to learn a lot more about curve adjustment -- I don''t generally mess around with it. You have not only ribboned with an iPhone camera, but one that is a couple of generations old. Nicely done, Mary Ann.', '2015-05-29 08:42:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7358228, 1150119, 5705, '<td valign="top">TY very much jgirl57</td>', 'TY very much jgirl57', '2015-06-07 20:23:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7380135, 1149800, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>LOL I just had a funny thought. Since both of you are laying in a mud puddle facing each other, he''s probably telling himself...man that''s the biggest frog I''ve ever seen. The shot is not bad/ I like the dof. Your focus on the frog and nothing else is good. The green in the foreground is a bit distracting though. That''s not a major problem for me but it probably hurt your score. Happy shooting</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... LOL I just had a funny thought. Since both of you are laying in a mud puddle facing each other, he''s probably telling himself...man that''s the biggest frog I''ve ever seen. The shot is not bad/ I like the dof. Your focus on the frog and nothing else is good. The green in the foreground is a bit distracting though. That''s not a major problem for me but it probably hurt your score. Happy shooting', '2015-07-02 13:04:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7380261, 1149881, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>Very strong skyline shot. I am assuming that this is Montreal. I like the reflections on the water. That is a very nice detail. The light on the top of the building to the right is a little bit glaring but that is not a big issue with me. Otherwise I think you did an excellent job.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... Very strong skyline shot. I am assuming that this is Montreal. I like the reflections on the water. That is a very nice detail. The light on the top of the building to the right is a little bit glaring but that is not a big issue with me. Otherwise I think you did an excellent job.', '2015-07-02 14:27:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7380506, 1150141, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>I like it. It has that element of fear in it. The dog has that vicious I''m gonna eat you look. The grass in the foreground also adds to the shot. 5.2 not a bad score for this. Happy shooting</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... I like it. It has that element of fear in it. The dog has that vicious I''m gonna eat you look. The grass in the foreground also adds to the shot. 5.2 not a bad score for this. Happy shooting', '2015-07-02 16:51:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7380516, 1150108, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings (again) from the Critique club<br/> <br/>We''ve run out of fresh images to critique, so now there are some old ones in the queue.<br/> <br/>You did extremely well with this particular shot Janine, I love it when those last minute attempts do better than we could ever expect.  <br/> <br/>This was one of my favourites in this challenge.  I loved the simplicity and really liked the texture (assuming Analogue Pro?)  I don''t have an iPhone any more but I do find that sometimes I get better angles when using the phone over the "big gun" not sure why :)<br/> <br/>Not too much to comment on this one, it''s a well done image<br/></td>', 'Greetings (again) from the Critique club We''ve run out of fresh images to critique, so now there are some old ones in the queue. You did extremely well with this particular shot Janine, I love it when those last minute attempts do better than we could ever expect.   This was one of my favourites in this challenge.  I loved the simplicity and really liked the texture (assuming Analogue Pro?)  I don''t have an iPhone any more but I do find that sometimes I get better angles when using the phone over the "big gun" not sure why :) Not too much to comment on this one, it''s a well done image', '2015-07-02 16:57:14.000000', NULL, 0);
